# Secrets
.env

# Runtime state: caches, usage ledger, calibrated thresholds, feedback
.runtime/

# The ~350 MB corpus IS committed, via Git LFS (see .gitattributes), so the repo is runnable
# straight after a clone. Worth knowing: GitHub's free LFS allowance is 1 GB of storage and
# 1 GB of bandwidth a month, and a full clone pulls ~350 MB of that — about three clones a
# month. If that ever becomes a problem, move the bundle to a GitHub Release asset, which has
# no bandwidth quota.
#
# Transient LanceDB bookkeeping — no value in version control.
data/legal_db/**/_transactions/
#
# _deletions/ is NOT transient and must stay committed. The table manifest names its deletion
# files by path, so a clone without them cannot open the database at all — it fails with
# "Not found: …/_deletions/0-2-….arrow" on the first query, long after the corpus check has
# happily reported 299 MB present. It is 762 bytes. Ignoring it cost a deployment.

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/

# Crawl4AI's own cache
.crawl4ai/

# Editors / OS
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
